# Octet's checks read Octet's own source and match it against patterns written with "\n":
# 59 of the 99 check files do. A clone on Windows with git's default core.autocrlf=true
# gets CRLF in the working tree, and five of them fail before a line has been changed
# (cursor, filesafety, pagefit, projects and purpose).
#
# Normalising to LF in the working tree on every platform keeps the checks meaningful and
# costs Windows nothing: Node, PowerShell and every editor in use read LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
